{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness","id":1122801,"title":"Your City in the Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-30T14:02:02-07:00","id":1122801,"title":"Your City in the Darkness","content":"So because I love writing up for Philly and I'm liking YMitC's Savannah work, let's put this one out to the people. Your city, your small corner of the world. Who runs the place? What's the supernatural setup? Who are the power players and what is the big struggle that makes it unique?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T16:25:27-07:00","id":1122834,"title":"","content":"I did a write up of San Diego for Urban Shadows, which is a setting-light urban fantasy game. Would anyone want to see that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T16:29:17-07:00","id":1122835,"title":"","content":"I think NYC is probably already covered in the existing material (believe the Seers have it). But since I live outside of NYC in Westchester, I wonder if they still control that area...<br /> <br /> That said, I'm only really well-versed in Changeling, so I'm not sure I could really do Westchester justice. Plus, I have a hard time figuring out how mages don't just win every time, unless it's all down to the infighting and Paradox","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-30-2017, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T16:30:31-07:00","id":1122836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1122834#post1122834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a write up of San Diego for Urban Shadows, which is a setting-light urban fantasy game. Would anyone want to see that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally would. What do you mean by &quot;setting-light&quot; though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T17:00:48-07:00","id":1122849,"title":"","content":"Edinburgh is one of the most haunted cities in Europe, the site of grave robberies due to the medical schools' demand for cadavers (and of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burke_and_Hare_murders\" target=\"_blank\">Burke and Hare</a> being too lazy to rob graves so they started murdering people to keep up with demand) and high society <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Weir\" target=\"_blank\">witch trials</a>, the birthplace of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Louis_Stevenson\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Louis Stevenson</a> and an influence on the <b>Strange Case Of Dr. Jekyll And Mister Hyde</b> and the university where <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_William_Polidori\" target=\"_blank\">Dr. Polidori</a> trained, and the local bus route includes <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosslyn_Chapel\" target=\"_blank\">Rosslyn Chapel</a> and the place where Dolly the sheep was cloned. In <b>The Chronicles Of Darkness</b> it's also home to Ashwood Abbey - who I imagine spending quite a lot of their time just dealing with the high incidence of weirdness in the local area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T17:16:42-07:00","id":1122852,"title":"","content":"I did my home of Orlando as a Demon-focused city.<br /> <br /> _________________<br /> <br /> <i>Way down south, an old custom dictates that if someone comes up to you on Christmas Day and says &quot;Christmas gift&quot; before y'all do, why y'all are obliged to give that person a present. Mind you, the custom does not say what sort of present y'all should give! But those of us who hail from the South consider ourselves to be gentlefolk. The gifts given and received in this manner are good enough to keep the custom alive and well.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Now, this is not to say that this custom does not have its drawbacks. Why, the Devil himself got a hold of the eastern coast of Florida in this manner! The Devil, being a canny fellow, knew that God was walking about Florida one Christmas Day, so he hid himself behind a stump. When the Lord came strolling by, the Devil jumped out real fast and said: &quot;Christmas gift!&quot; And the Lord, being as fine a Southern gentleman as you could meet, held up to his end of the custom and told the Devil, &quot;You can have the east coast,&quot; and continued his stroll. So now the Devil plays hurricane games with the east coast of Florida whenever it pleases.</i><br /> <br /> The Devil's Tree. The Devil's Millhopper. The Devil's Chair. Hole. Den. Eye. Florida is, much like the midwest, carpeted in frightening places said to be the domain of evil. This isn't too surprising \u2013 fifteen minutes of walking in any direction in Florida will run you into quicksand, a poisonous animal, a poisonous plant, or muck that looks like two inches of water, but is in reality ten feet of decayed plant and animal matter. The state has no real mosquito season \u2013 they're all year round \u2013 and out of the seven or so venomous snake genera that live in North America, Florida has six. Explorers would come up over the next ridge expecting to see the paradise described by the first settlers, only to drown in the swamp. Edible plants are everywhere, but nearly all of the water is tainted in some way. Florida has been said to lead to \u201cgreen death,\u201d where the nature of the swamp, the overwhelming and oppressive heat and humidity, along with the proliferation of low-nutrition and toxic plants lead to starvation and dehydration while surrounded by bounty. The first settlers, paleo-indians, arrived fourteen thousand years ago, and ate nearly nothing but shellfish. Between alligator, gar, snakes, amoeba of varying types, and the churning miasma of every ooze and sap from every tree and rotting animal carcass all the way up to New York filtering down into the state's bogs and swamps, nothing else in the water really seems worth it.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, the state has a long history of blood, Spanish, Native, White, Hispanic, Black \u2013 you name it, someone has fought and died for their own little patch of leech-ridden mud and buried the evidence beneath the rigid cypress trees. The region has been continuously populated for nearly fourteen thousand years, and in that time, the grinding gears of slavery and oppression have consistently layered themselves over the top of each exchange of power. Indian refugees, escaped slaves, criminals, and those of less troublesome make but still wishing to hide from the gaping, hungry maw of civilization would lose themselves in the reeds and oaks even well past statehood \u2013 it remained largely unlivable swamp until the proliferation of air conditioning, well up into the middle of World War II, when land speculators were promised low-cost patches of land, only to discover they'd bought a pit in the stinking swamps.<br /> <br /> That isn't to say Florida is without its fair shake of much less terrible legend \u2013 the fountain of youth is reportedly here, somewhere. The skunk ape haunts the backwoods from Myakka all the way down to the Everglades and is reported to steal beans. Love bugs were genetically engineered to fight mosquitoes, and the National UFO Reporting Center and MUFON continue to list Florida as a sighting hotspot almost as baked as Mexico City. There's no mountains visible anywhere in the state. There's just about no place you can go to see over the trees, and where you can, they're putting up houses to block that view. No matter where you are, in the woods or the city, there's always a fence of some kind blocking the view, and the only thing on the horizon is the sky and a line like somebody drew it with a ruler.<br /> <br /> God loves Florida; wilderness butts right up against civilization. Alligators snack on mussels and tourists right underneath office buildings, and when one actually does wander into a crowded area, they'll just come around to tape up the legs like a busted ride and let people take pictures like it's a big puppet on a stick and haul it off to God-knows-where. When you do buy gator meat, it's in little fried chunks. Could be anything. Trees form barriers around nice little golf courses and flat expanses of grass. The state's lost the battle to the fire ants, and there's always something else out there in the woods and swamps. Anacondas loose, monkeys, some guy says his brother knows a tourist that got eaten by a tiger, and it's always just two blocks away from where the kids are playing or the gang is selling their shit. Take one step in and there's skulls and discarded beer bottles right there. The grape vines and the air potatoes are like one glorious perfect fence growing over cypress trees and clusters of rusted pipes sticking up out of the ground. By contrast, the city's always thick with new projects and faded glamor. Stick to the main streets, and everything looks great, but step off the path and it's like you just walked by the \u201cemployees only\u201d signs and found the dilapidated break room, the broken machines, the workers hiding behind the screens and wiggling the fake birds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T21:06:02-07:00","id":1122894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1122836#post1122836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally would. What do you mean by &amp;quot;setting-light&amp;quot; though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Urban Shadows itself doesn't have lore; it gives you playbooks for most common supernatural types and leaves it at that.<br /> <br /> Here it is, as a WIP <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bFhwKiy0paErvA1R-9IcXrZRulg259BUh_6OqzJg4j4\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...9BUh_6OqzJg4j4</a> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T21:16:45-07:00","id":1122897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1122894#post1122894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Urban Shadows itself doesn't have lore; it gives you playbooks for most common supernatural types and leaves it at that.<br /> <br /> Here it is, as a WIP <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bFhwKiy0paErvA1R-9IcXrZRulg259BUh_6OqzJg4j4\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...9BUh_6OqzJg4j4</a> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a really cool setting, Lex! If I was doing a San Diego game I'd probably use that as my foundation, and add whatever little bits about San Diego were mentioned in <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>. I've got a writeup for my hometown (and current residence) of Winnipeg filed away somewhere, I'll see if I can spruce it up for this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T21:29:07-07:00","id":1122900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1122897#post1122897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That is a really cool setting, Lex! If I was doing a San Diego game I'd probably use that as my foundation, and add whatever little bits about San Diego were mentioned in <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>. I've got a writeup for my hometown (and current residence) of Winnipeg filed away somewhere, I'll see if I can spruce it up for this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me started on how excruciatingly wrong Secrets got this town. A shootout with an armed militia, in one of the most progressive cities in the state with the strictest gun laws? Pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T21:48:15-07:00","id":1122904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1122900#post1122900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't get me started on how excruciatingly wrong Secrets got this town. A shootout with an armed militia, in one of the most progressive cities in the state with the strictest gun laws? Pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>In which case I'll just ignore that part of Secrets of the Covenants except as a look at how the Invictus do things, and just use your writeup instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T21:54:45-07:00","id":1122908,"title":"","content":"Denver is pretty well covered in Hunting Ground: the Rockies. But that is over 10 years old at this point. I'd love to do an update to the setting for 2017, even if doing so would be a little on the metaplotty side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T22:01:10-07:00","id":1122910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1122900#post1122900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't get me started on how excruciatingly wrong Secrets got this town. A shootout with an armed militia, in one of the most progressive cities in the state with the strictest gun laws? Pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was meant to be a leftist militia, like in that one hit-man level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T22:10:53-07:00","id":1122911,"title":"","content":"I'm in the middle of writing up Sydney as a crossover setting with inspiration from the Demon Seed Collection. The main focus is examining what parts of your identify are you willing to give up to try and achieve your dreams, and examining multiculturalism to a degree by asking how much of your identity determines your future.<br /> <br /> Main focus creature wise is on Vampires, Demons, and Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 07-31-2017, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T22:24:00-07:00","id":1122912,"title":"","content":"I usually do Miami, but the last one was years ago and ended up with a huge shake-up. Series of new vampire princes and then a vampire declaring himself king and making it clear he was going expansionist. Werewolves, decimated by a Pure and Forsaken battle, with survivors picked off by Bale Hounds and hunters organized under another Bale Hound, were finally making their way back to the city in a sort of 'gold rush.' Mages, victims of other hunters, were for the most part absent. I never really bothered fleshing out many of the other gamelines beyond a few individuals, most don't really have communities and the Changelings kept hidden. The Sin-Eaters were all Nazis and neo-Nazis and lived offshore.<br /> <br /> Should probably update it, maybe I'll wait for Deviant but I get the feeling they're not big on communities either. Based on what little we know there would be more than a few, though.<br /> <br /> We switched to another area for werewolf, then I stuck with it, or nearby at least, for mage. That's more of a broad area with a <i>dark secret</i>, sort of like the Boston one but I've only got mages there and the other gamelines are invisible to the point that at least one of the mages didn't think they existed. There is a group of Beasts on an island, but they're all either Rampant or mad and under the control of one of the Earthbound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T22:27:01-07:00","id":1122913,"title":"","content":"I have idea how to run city of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lublin\" target=\"_blank\">Lublin, Poland</a> in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>. It's rather intellectual, collage place on the crossroads of Europe now, that rose from mass work sites of previous Poland governing system ( PRL ) into European city it once was in XV-XVII century. City motto is <i>'City of Inspiration' </i>and on that, I was envisioning it as mostly <b>Mage</b> and <b>Changeling</b> setting. There is universal Mystery in it - at least once in lifetime, citizens of Lublin have a Dream - vision so profound, it's move their life. It can be dream about deep issue - love, work, education, anything important, really - but it seems as like every who live here most of it's life, have one.<br /> <br /> Awakened are not more than up to 50 sorceresses, fighting mostly for the new minds of students on 5 Universities in Lublin, almost Seers free. Changelings, on the other hand, are divided in to two Freeholds - Western one is about Four Seasons, traditional Freehold of Western Europe. Smaller, Eastern one, is about Slavic Courts of Night &amp; Day. All those groups are looking in to 'City of Inspiration' Mystery, from their own perspective.<br /> <br /> In city there is also infamous Nazi extermination camp - <a href=\"https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campo_de_concentraci%C3%B3n_de_Majdanek\" target=\"_blank\">Majdanek</a>. ( I even live 2 kilometers from it ). This kind of place of great pain, torture and sorrow is surely Shadow Realm Wound in <b>CoD</b>, even when nowdays it's more like painful museum and tourist place ( we all the time have tours from Israel ). What's even more disturbing is that near the site is modern cemetery, that I envision will have very roused ghost of the dead by it. ( My uncle is even buried on this place, near death camp. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-31-2017, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T22:41:26-07:00","id":1122917,"title":"","content":"I ran a jokey one shot in my small town where two freshly escaped Changelings are greeted by the Autumn and Spring Kings saying &quot;Finally, someone to represent Summer and Winter&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T05:27:48-07:00","id":1122980,"title":"","content":"I'm (very slowly) writing the supernatural set up for Rome, as you can see from my signature. <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i> (and <i>Requiem for Rome</i>, obviously) have something to say about my city, but the only thing that directly contradicts what I've written is that the Prince of Rome is canonically a man, while my setting has a female Gangrel Prince. I did my write up years before the release of the book, so things could have changed in my setting, if you want. The position of the Prince was very shaky, so that is very much a possibility.<br /> <br /> I've ideas for both Mage and Changeling, but I haven't written anything yet. Since &quot;all the roads lead to Rome&quot; one of the main Mysteries of the setting will be the state of Rome as a &quot;City of Doors&quot; not unlike Sigil from Planescape, with lots of conflict between &quot;natives&quot; and people coming from all over the world. For Changeling I'd like a Court system based on the minor Arcana, so there would be a Gold (which is how Italians call the Pentacle suit), Cups, Swords and Wands Court, since our card games use the tarots as a playing deck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T05:55:45-07:00","id":1122987,"title":"","content":"<b>BARCELONA:</b><br /> <br /> <b>- Vampire:</b> Ruled by Javier Montoya, an Ordo Dracul Prince since about 100 years ago. The other covenants have a lot of strong internal divisions, so he has supported some factions of those covensnts in exchange for their support in his princedom. Montoya is obsessed with Dragon Nests snd Ley Lines from Barcelona, specially in the one from Sagrada Familia, the strongest he's found and where he believes there is an ancient mystical power slumbering and waiting to awake.<br /> <br /> <b>- Werewolf:</b> An unofficial protectorate ruled by a coalition of two Lodges, one Forsaken (Lodge of St. Jordi) and one Pure (Order of the Dragonslayers) with the same Patron, an spirit of catalan culture called the Dragonslayer with s very strong symbolism related to St George (Saint Patron of Catalonia). Both defend catalan culture and have implanted an apartheid model against spanish werewolves (specially by the Ivory Claws, the Forsaken are more tolerant).*<br /> * For those who know about it, that's not any metaphore or paralelism with real live in Catalonia. It's just one idea I thought appropiate for Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <b>- Mage:</b> Libertine Dictatorship. During Spanish Civil War, the Seers made a great successful offensive in all rhe country. The Barcelona Counsilium decided they couldn't save the city and ordered to abandone it, saving whatever could be saved and destroying the rest. But Free Councilers (and some members of the other Orders) decided to resist, and against all the odds, they won and broke the siege (bring the Battle of Barcelona one of the most cheered events of European Libertines).<br /> After that, they refused to return power to the Consilium and stablished a Libertine Assembly to rule the city. During 60 years, under the guidance and counsel of Seimei, a Japanese Libertine (see Free Council book) the Assambky worked and respected the orders. But after her death, a young charismatic radical called Serrallonga, has become the &quot;first citizen&quot; of the Assambly and has converted it in a tiranny of the masses, exiling, punishing and &quot;disappearing&quot; any who publicy opposes to its decissions. In response, a cabal of young Thearchs, Els Cadells (The Cubs) have initiated a resistence movement againstthe Libertines for restoring the freedom for the Awakened from Barcelona.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 07-31-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T08:49:22-07:00","id":1123032,"title":"","content":"Heh, I should do that at some point for the little village in Germany I come from. I'd add in a lot of weirdness - we have a few things that lend itself for this here. the local castle, which as was recently uncovered must have been much older than originally assumed, what with the base upon which the newer layers were built being from before 1000 A.D. (wonder what else they uncovered and don't speak about? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), a similarly old church site, and some local history (World War 2 especially) that could be made use of are in place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T09:32:05-07:00","id":1123043,"title":"","content":"I wrote a half a Geist themed London ages ago. But if you look at the Lord Stewards in Dream Catchers, that would give you a pretty good idea of how I'd write a crossover London. I imagine London itself would focus more on the multi-culturalism side of Vampires, Werewolves, Changelings, and more all compromising to live together. Where as outside of London a bit more focus is given to the maintaining traditions side of things.<br /> <br /> London really is another country from the rest of the UK. (Well, maybe not Cambridge - the other place I've lived)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-31-2017, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/m