rse has a bigger population there, so as to make it easier to hide supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T12:28:37-07:00","id":1123111,"title":"","content":"double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-31-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T12:43:28-07:00","id":1123122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1123110#post1123110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Then I'm assuming that the alternate universe has a bigger population there, so as to make it easier to hide supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, everyone there is Supernatural, you just don't know which kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-31-2017, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T13:27:31-07:00","id":1123148,"title":"","content":"I have actually tried a number of times to think about how my city may show up in the CofD- but usually, it feels like some sort of &quot;evil caricature&quot;. Maybe because it is the lack of urban legends or similar stories about it. When I'll have an idea, I'll post it in here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T13:45:22-07:00","id":1123156,"title":"","content":"I definitely have the advantage of Washington Irving's stories, but those all tend towards fae stuff in my mind. Well, ghosts too, but we all know how conflated those two can get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T14:47:17-07:00","id":1123185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1122835#post1122835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think NYC is probably already covered in the existing material (believe the Seers have it). But since I live outside of NYC in Westchester, I wonder if they still control that area...<br /> <br /> That said, I'm only really well-versed in Changeling, so I'm not sure I could really do Westchester justice. Plus, I have a hard time figuring out how mages don't just win every time, unless it's all down to the infighting and Paradox</div> </div> </div> </div>In my game I have outside of NYC between large cities I have what I call the strange where random horrors exist between the cities. I know in westchester I have a bunch of demons and werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T14:54:53-07:00","id":1123187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1123185#post1123185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my game I have outside of NYC between large cities I have what I call the strange where random horrors exist between the cities. I know in westchester I have a bunch of demons and werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dunno. There's few places I've been too where you can't at least hear a highway. Not sure I could see too much room for random horrors to hide in even my relatively well-forested neck of the woods<br /> <br /> Unrelated, but do your Westchester Werewolves look more Coyotes or wild Dogs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T15:32:37-07:00","id":1123200,"title":"","content":"I've been working on a Demon story set in Champaign, Illinois. The university is good concealment for a lot of Infrastructure, including cryptoflora corn and a small ring of well-intentioned Integrators called the Geek Squad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T15:38:58-07:00","id":1123203,"title":"","content":"Still working on this one ... <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/662429-the-city\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...62429-the-city</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T15:41:55-07:00","id":1123205,"title":"","content":"Don't underestimate the dangers of the road. The Smoke-Drinker and his Thousand Steel Teeth. That Which Is Broken, Walkerbreaker and the Rest Stop Killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T15:43:25-07:00","id":1123207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1123187#post1123187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I dunno. There's few places I've been too where you can't at least hear a highway. Not sure I could see too much room for random horrors to hide in even my relatively well-forested neck of the woods<br /> <br /> Unrelated, but do your Westchester Werewolves look more Coyotes or wild Dogs?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I should have said werecreatures. They are werecoyotes and foxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T15:46:18-07:00","id":1123209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1123110#post1123110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Then I'm assuming that the alternate universe has a bigger population there, so as to make it easier to hide supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> In the alternate universe, while a few other events went differently, leading to increasing populations after WW2, the big one is that one of the town's entrepreneurs when it was called Miday, Collins Hirsch, was wounded in 1918 and spent six weeks in the back of an ambulance, talking to the driver about his hometown and wanting to do something great for it.<br /> <br /> His driver was Walt Disney, who contacted him in the 1960s after being told he had to &quot;wait&quot; to build EPCOT.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7v_jlttUwAOUmQzZC00aVZpU0k/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">I made a whole wiki entry for the &quot;mortal&quot; part of town</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T16:01:12-07:00","id":1123212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1123207#post1123207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well I should have said werecreatures. They are werecoyotes and foxes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, like Changing Breeds werecoyotes and werefoxes? Or Uratha and Pure that look like coyotes and foxes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T16:04:17-07:00","id":1123214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1123205#post1123205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't underestimate the dangers of the road. The Smoke-Drinker and his Thousand Steel Teeth. That Which Is Broken, Walkerbreaker and the Rest Stop Killer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh I see. You were talking to me. Yeah, point taken. Those one-lane back roads can be pretty scary even in real life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T16:56:20-07:00","id":1123232,"title":"","content":"I've made copious notes for a Changeling game set in Glasgow.<br /> <br /> As the Dear Green Place, or the Green Hollow, it's positively riddled through with trods and gates into the Hedge. Lots of Scottish myths about the Fair Folk and their wiles would come into play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T20:34:26-07:00","id":1123294,"title":"","content":"There's a suburb of Houston known as the Woodlands. It's about an hour or so north of the city proper, and it's aptly named: trees are everywhere, towering over the roads, looming along running paths, ringing golf courses and dividing neighborhoods, and all those neighborhoods well-to-do or better. It's the home for the sort of people who can afford a long commute into work, or working from home, or the best sort of schools for their kids, and its east side is dominated by a mall so large that people will come in from miles around just to shop.<br /> <br /> If half the stories I've heard about it are true, as a former resident currently living on the other side of the tracks (literally), it'd make one hell of a Vampire setting. Undead thrill-seekers hurtling down the roads at night, confident that they'll survive whatever crash might come; wealthy members of the Invictus and the Lancea et Sanctum who are too self-assured and &quot;discerning&quot; to descend to living in the city itself; ghouls hiding out among the predominately non-white lawn care crews; and always, the necessity of keeping up with the Draculas. Gotta show that you've got just as much in your undeath as anybody else.<br /> <br /> (Admittedly, I know none of the stories I've heard are true, and the Woodlands is, by and large, a very nice place- but it's tempting to look at it and ask: what if?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12958-raz_fox","name":"Raz_Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T23:38:08-07:00","id":1123332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1123212#post1123212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, like Changing Breeds werecoyotes and werefoxes? Or Uratha and Pure that look like coyotes and foxes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing Breeds but I changed most of the background to make fit into the world better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T11:29:32-07:00","id":1123567,"title":"","content":"Anyone know a good free GIS system for layered mapping. Been wanting to do Houston by Night for ages but the thing about Houston, especially if you talking the greater Houston area is its frikin immense. In traffic it can take as long to drive from one side to the other going straight through as it does in some states to hit 2 opposite borders. Tried using Google earth but got frustrated. H-town is truly awesome and needs to be a melting pot setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:49:10-07:00","id":1123927,"title":"","content":"Well I live in Seattle sooo... Pretty much already covered in the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T11:03:41-07:00","id":1123937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1123927#post1123927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I live in Seattle sooo... Pretty much already covered in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about your own spin though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T21:53:25-07:00","id":1124173,"title":"","content":"Bedford Indiana. Very little to do, if you live here you're either retired, or trying to find a way to get out. Very little in the way of things to do, has a wal-mart, a starbucks, a mcdonalds. parked up right against a highway to so all the business huddle up close in hopes to get their fill of that sweet interstate highway travellers income. I imagine there's a pack of werewolves that keep territory here, the odd Sin-Eater chilling out, and changelings have a healthy community (well as healthy a community you can have in a town hemming closer to the midwestern-south)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T10:19:58-07:00","id":1124354,"title":"","content":"I created my home city of Miami for a Mage game, and it spread into other splats as well, ranging from Were-Gators in the Everglades, to a Changeling Court representing the 4 winds in Key West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T10:24:32-07:00","id":1124359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1124354#post1124354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I created my home city of Miami for a Mage game, and it spread into other splats as well, ranging from Were-Gators in the Everglades, to a Changeling Court representing the 4 winds in Key West.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did the Miami setting in Changeling 1e cover Key West?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T10:25:48-07:00","id":1124362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1124359#post1124359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Did the Miami setting in Changeling 1e cover Key West?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to my knowledge. I got into Changeling during its 2e spoilers, finding that more palatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T10:32:34-07:00","id":1124366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1124362#post1124362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not to my knowledge. I got into Changeling during its 2e spoilers, finding that more palatable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Short story was that in 1999, the Summer Court ruler had staged a coup and instituted eternal Summer rule, exiling the Spring Court to the Everglades. Freehold's on the brink of war as the True Fae circle and grumbling grows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T13:42:13-07:00","id":1124455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1124366#post1124366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Short story was that in 1999, the Summer Court ruler had staged a coup and instituted eternal Summer rule, exiling the Spring Court to the Everglades. Freehold's on the brink of war as the True Fae circle and grumbling grows.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very nice. For my story, the Court of 4 Winds is a small group of about 20 Changelings who keep to themselves in the Keys, safeguarding several reefs that actually have stable portals to the Hedge, and collaborating with a Magician of the Storm Keeper Legacy and his apprentice to protect the locals from powerful storms and floods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T13:56:44-07:00","id":1124462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1124455#post1124455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Very nice. For my story, the Court of 4 Winds is a small group of about 20 Changelings who keep to themselves in the Keys, safeguarding several reefs that actually have stable portals to the Hedge, and collaborating with a Magician of the Storm Keeper Legacy and his apprentice to protect the locals from powerful storms and floods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, that's pretty awesome. Could you tell me more about these courts, and how many Changelings are in each?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T14:03:49-07:00","id":1124463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1124462#post1124462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, that's pretty awesome. Could you tell me more about these courts, and how many Changelings are in each?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Each wind essentially functions like normal Seasonal Court in some way. The largest Court is the West Wind, Zephyrus, at about 9 members. Their version of Spring, centered around warmth and compassion. The smallest court was of Boreas, the North Wind. They represented a hybrid of Winter and Autumn, and have about 3 members now. They usually spike in numbers during times of famine and loss, like the orange plague in the 70's, Hurricane Andrew in '92, and recently Katrina and Wilma in the mid-2000's. The other two aren't as strong on average, and don't represent the Seasons as clearly, so they're often a place for Changelings who don't care for the hardline symbolism and narrative of the other Courts, preferring a more open ended system. Like a Choose-Your-Own-Adventure book for their politics. They're represented as the Winds Notus and Eurus, the oft-ignored ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:26:02-07:00","id":1124524,"title":"","content":"For the last year, I've lived just outside a town in Oxfordshire called Wallingford. It's an archetypal quaint English town. Agatha Christie once lived here and it's used to film <i>Midsomer Murders</i>. The ideals of the pastoral English murder genre might be enough for a changeling freehold, perhaps with symbiotic courts based on familiar charm/conformity/idyllic vs. scandal.<br /> <br /> There might be room for werewolves too. They would probably be mostly Ivory Claws here, but I think that Iron Masters in particular would be interested in the environmental (hydrology in particular) management research that goes on in the area. Think of the implications for river spirits, especially that of the Thames.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 08-03-2017, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T18:01:58-07:00","id":1124553,"title":"","content":"I have actually been working on a Bronx Geist Writeup and also a Baltimore Beast Setting. I will post links to both when I'm done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:25:16-07:00","id":1124759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1124524#post1124524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the last year, I've lived just outside a town in Oxfordshire called Wallingford. It's an archetypal quaint English town. Agatha Christie once lived here and it's used to film <i>Midsomer Murders</i>. The ideals of the pastoral English murder genre might be enough for a changeling freehold, perhaps with symbiotic courts based on familiar charm/conformity/idyllic vs. scandal.<br /> <br /> There might be room for werewolves too. They would probably be mostly Ivory Claws here, but I think that Iron Masters in particular would be interested in the environmental (hydrology in particular) management research that goes on in the area. Think of the implications for river spirits, especially that of the Thames.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a group of slashers?<br /> <br /> Seriously, after just one series/season of Midsummer, you can't tell me that there isn't a cabal of slashers out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T08:09:55-07:00","id":1124782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1124759#post1124759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about a group of slashers?<br /> <br /> Seriously, after just one series/season of Midsummer, you can't tell me that there isn't a cabal of slashers out there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or even just normal human thrill killers with connections. It's a proven fact that there are even more semi-mundane conspiracies in the CoD alongside the supernaturals and their hunters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:15:48-07:00","id":1124913,"title":"","content":"The Bale Hound who was the patron of the Ashwood Abbey in Miami was also the patron and organizer of the Hunt Club in my setting, the latter being a compact of Slashers. He was fun to play, based heavily off of Kraven the Hunter but far more debonair.<br /> <br /> There were a weird amount of slashers in the area, I should have come up with a reason for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:29:09-07:00","id":1124915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1124913#post1124913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were a weird amount of slashers in the area, I should have come up with a reason for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, one your players are supposed to find out, or something behind the scenes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:35:10-07:00","id":1124918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1124915#post1124915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, one your players are supposed to find out, or something behind the scenes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both, either. None of the players really would have been interested, except maybe the hunters. But even though we're not playing it right now, it's still a setting that's been built up through their adventures and so forth, who knows when they'll go back.<br /> <br /> Might fit for Deviant, there was a corporation they broke into that was working on AI and had a captured unchained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:35:29-07:00","id":1125238,"title":"","content":"My town is like 40k ... not much of supernatural feel to it .. maybe Forsaken? or Lost? but not much else i would think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T15:32:08-07:00","id":1125387,"title":"","content":"I grew up in London so I usually run my mage game in modern London. Haven't written it up but draw on a variety of sources including Neil Gaiman Neverwhere (mostly for Changling elements), David Aaronovitch Rivers of London urban fantasy series about modern mage working for Scotland Yard, and the Fireborn RPG from fantasy flight which was set in modern London and has lots of rpg inspiration in its GM guide. Cubicle 7 has source books for its Cthulhu britanica and World War Cthulhu lines set in 1930's and 1940's London which provides great background resources for major areas of London, as well as Chaosiums Cthulhu by Gaslight for Victorian era. All this provides good historical background although needs to be updated to modern period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T15:35:07-07:00","id":1125390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1125238#post1125238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My town is like 40k ... not much of supernatural feel to it .. maybe Forsaken? or Lost? but not much else i would think.</div> </div> </div> </div>But when you're running a game, where does it take place? What is your tables setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T15:39:53-07:00","id":1125391,"title":"","content":"I currently live in Corpus Christi TX (gulf coast south tx) and have wondered about using it as a setting a bit like the savage world setting of Pinebox TX revolving around a hunter cell of students at TX A and M Corpus Christi. South TX is very Hispanic so maybe could use some of the information from the nWoD Mexico sourcebook although I don't have that book so not sure how much is place specific as opposed to relating to more broad cultural and supernatural aspects that could be extended to south tx.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:28:47-07:00","id":1129655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122801-your-city-in-the-darkness?p=1125390#post1125390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But when you're running a game, where does it take place? What is your tables setting?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I use the City .. my super city that I am slowly developing ... Check my earlier post in the this topic .. the link is there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T10:58:59-07:00","id":1129881,"title":"","content":"I've been working on detailing Sydney as it stands in my personal Chronicles of Darkness for a while now, though I'm nowhere near done.<br /> <br /> The Vampires of Sydney are ruled by the Invictus, who are lead by Prince Robert Jones, who was Embraced shortly after the founding of the city by the original Duke of Sydney. The majority of the Vampiric population stand with them.<br /> The Lancea Et Sanctum tried to take over the domain in the early nineties, but they've been brought to heel under a puppet Bishop who's managed to keep them under control. There aren't that many of them any more, though they were once more numerous.<br /> The various faiths that comprise the Circle of the Crone can never agree on much, meaning that their faction has little in the way of influence despite a fairly large population.<br /> The Ordo Dracul stick to themselves and are even more secretive than they are in other parts of the world, but have strong ties with the Invictus. They've got a large population, but nobody outside of their ranks knows exactly how large.<br /> The Carthian Movement maintains a significant powerbase in Western Sydney, but usually go out of their way to appear peaceful. They present a united front to outsiders, while in truth being wracked by internal conflict between those who want a Democratic Republic, those who support a Direct Democracy and those who seek to bring Communism to the Kindred of Sydney.<br /> The city is currently suffering from a notable Kindred overpopulation crisis, which has lead to the Prince putting in place exceedingly strict laws regarding the Embrace and the Masquerade. VII is also becoming active in the city, with the murders growing more and more frequent each month. All of this puts the Kindred of Sydney on edge.<br /> <br /> The Seers of the Throne have been the predominant power among Sydney's Awakened since the Epopt of the local Guardian Caucus defected in the late eighties, though resistance against them has been gradually growing.<br /> The leaders of each local Diamond Caucus (with the notable exception of the Guardians of the Veil) sit on the Tribunal of Sydney, which demands a lot more from its constituents than a typical Consilium, but also affords more protection. The Adamantine Arrow commands the most power, naturally.<br /> The Libertines are banded together under the S.E.A.L. Assembly, which stretches throughout most of New South Wales and the Australian Capital Territory. S.E.A.L. supposedly stands for 'South East Australian Libertines', but the Assembly's members like to joke about other potential meanings.<br /> The city doesn't have a single big Mystery, but rather a large number of smaller ones.<br /> <br /> Due to some of the area's supernatural quirks, the True Fae and their Huntsmen find it especially difficult to enter Sydney. This has attracted a very large and active Changeling population. This expansive Freehold largely follows the Seasonal Court system, although a fifth secretive 'Court of Cycles' has also established itself, working to ensure that the proper rituals are preformed to maintain the barrier that protects the city. In addition, a small nomadic Freehold occasionally makes port in Sydney Harbour.<br /> <br /> I don't know what to do about other supernaturals just yet, but yeah.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type"